    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0271" n="143" xml:id="pg143"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 99.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1885-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 10, 1885</date>. (Received November 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 429.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt; on the 8th instant, of your instruction No. 285 of the 1st ultimo. In
                    compliance therewith, I have advised the minister for foreign affairs of
                    Honduras by telegraph that steps have been taken to prevent the departure of any
                    expedition against that Republic in violation of the neutrality laws of the
                    United States.</p>
                <p>By telegram of this date the minister, in reply, expresses the grateful
                    acknowledgments of his Government. I inclose copies and translations of the
                    telegrams referred to.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENEY C. HALL.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d99-a1.xml" xpointer="d99-a1"/>
